drg: eMMC root writes (CMD24), opt-in with emmcrw=1

Built on the shim R6 write test (drg/BOOTLOG.md #15): CMD24 with one
64-bit ADMA2 descriptor wrote a block 8 GiB past the iOS image in
userdata, R1 0x900, read back equal, original restored.

Writes stay off (EROFS) unless boot-arg emmcrw=1, and are checked
against the partition both in strategy and per sector right before the
command. At start the driver reads EXT_CSD (CMD8) and prints the
partition access and cache state: writes need the user area selected
(if EXT_CSD cannot be read the disk stays read-only, never fails),
and if the volatile cache is on, DKIOCSYNCHRONIZE and B_FUA flush it
with CMD6 FLUSH_CACHE (R1b).

